From: omaspace <omaspace@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 18:20:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] omarchy: owner-qualified apps for Hyprland agent input

Read ~/.config/cua-driver/qualified-apps (<package> <version|*> <exe>)
and admit those executables exactly like the built-in Inkscape and
LibreOffice entries: live /proc exe must match, owned by that installed
pacman package. Unlisted apps stay client_not_qualified.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../src/wayland/hyprland_compatibility.rs     | 98 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 88 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libs/cua-driver/rust/crates/platform-linux/src/wayland/hyprland_compatibility.rs b/libs/cua-driver/rust/crates/platform-linux/src/wayland/hyprland_compatibility.rs
index 5d14aeb..2c3d210 100644
--- a/libs/cua-driver/rust/crates/platform-linux/src/wayland/hyprland_compatibility.rs
+++ b/libs/cua-driver/rust/crates/platform-linux/src/wayland/hyprland_compatibility.rs
@@ -5,13 +5,13 @@
 use std::io::Read;
 use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};
 
-struct QualifiedPackage {
-    name: &'static str,
-    version: &'static str,
-    executable: &'static str,
+struct QualifiedPackage<'a> {
